                 READ THE FUCKING SCOPES.

  Hand your agents the keys. Try not to fucking pwn yourself.

[ INSTALL NOTES ]

  One binary. Run it directly, or verify its SHA-256 and use install.sh.
  The installer refuses an existing binary unless you explicitly force it.
  It does not replace your credential file, rules, or shell profile.

  Testing next to an existing setup? Use BOTH --config-dir and --state-dir
  with separate paths. README.md has a copy-ready isolated demo command.

[ READ THIS BEFORE YOU PWN YOURSELF ]

  Broad keys can delete infrastructure, spend money, publish, send mail,
  and commit as you. That's the point. Scope is not fucking decoration.

  The file is plaintext, mode 0600. Your user and unrestricted agents can
  read it. No sandbox. No spending limiter. No undo fairy. A saved live
  key does not authorize live charges. Don't post your fucking .env.

  Commands launched with `run` get only the selected keys plus basic
  process context. Their output is NOT filtered. Know what you're running.

[ PICARD MODE ]

  godmode picard link     original YTMND URL
  godmode picard open     open the original in your browser
  godmode picard play     play the original excerpt on repeat
  godmode picard stop     stop Godmode's player

  In the board: p = play/stop, v = original source. Nothing autoplays.
  First play fetches the approximately eight-second YTMND loop. It does
  not read your credentials. The recording is not included in this release.
  Use the same --state-dir when stopping a player started with an override.

